嗯，你知道，温迪有很多优点。

00:09:54.200 --> 00:09:57.120
Well, you know, there's so many things that are great about Wendy.
干得好。

00:09:57.760 --> 00:09:58.080
Way to go.
我深深地爱着她。

00:09:58.520 --> 00:09:59.960
And I love her dearly.
干得好。

00:10:00.300 --> 00:10:00.600
Way to go.
但有时她的脾气确实有待提高。

00:10:01.920 --> 00:10:06.840
But her temper leaves something to be desired sometimes.
偶尔。

00:10:07.780 --> 00:10:08.380
Every once in a while.
绝不可能。

00:10:08.920 --> 00:10:09.160
No way.
你说什么？

00:10:09.330 --> 00:10:10.100
What do you say?
什么？

00:10:10.640 --> 00:10:11.120
What?
他说的是脾气。

00:10:11.380 --> 00:10:12.440
He says temper.
好吧。

00:10:13.180 --> 00:10:13.700
All right.
嗯，我想过那个问题，这是我认为我需要改进的地方。

00:10:13.700 --> 00:10:18.420
Well, I thought about that question, and this is what I thought I need to improve on.
代数。

00:10:21.060 --> 00:10:21.540
Algebra.
代数。

00:10:22.780 --> 00:10:23.260
Algebra.
你怎么能漏掉那个？

00:10:23.300 --> 00:10:24.660
How could you miss that?
你怎么能忽视这一点？

00:10:25.120 --> 00:10:27.160
How did you overlook that?
我不知道。

00:10:27.690 --> 00:10:28.260
I don't know.
我们其实讨论过这个。

00:10:28.300 --> 00:10:29.580
We actually talked about that.
我必须说，最奇怪的事情之一是，在大多数婚礼上，你从来看不到人们有任何形式的不和。

00:10:29.580 --> 00:10:35.780
I have to say, also, one of the things that's so odd is that at most weddings you never see people have any kind of discord.
对。

00:10:36.720 --> 00:10:36.820
Yeah.
我的梦想是，我们正惨遭滑铁卢（而这很不凑巧地真的发生了），每个人都以为我们结不成婚了，而最后一个问题是一个真正极其困难的问题，我们俩必须都答对才能结婚。

00:10:37.340 --> 00:10:49.680
My dream would have been that we were just failing miserably, which oddly enough happened, and that everybody thought we weren't going to be able to get married, and the last question was just a truly impossible question that we both had to get right in order to get married.
而且有些人真的以为我们办不成了。

00:10:50.240 --> 00:10:52.900
And there were some people who didn't think we were going to pull it off.
有些人以为我们挺不过去。

00:10:52.940 --> 00:10:54.780
There were some people who thought we weren't going to make it.
我觉得——我是说，我只看过这个的录像带——但我很难相信人们会信以为真。

00:10:55.400 --> 00:11:01.280
I find that, I mean, I've only seen the videotape of this, but I find it hard to believe that people would believe that.
嗯，你知道，我以前以为这很难让人相信，但我看着人们的脸，他们真的在想，好吧，我们该怎么办？

00:11:01.380 --> 00:11:07.900
Well, you know, I thought it was going to be hard to believe too, but I looked at people's faces and they were really, well, what are we going to do?
你现在打算怎么办？

00:11:07.940 --> 00:11:08.640
What are you going to do now?
哦，他们完全相信了。

00:11:09.620 --> 00:11:10.880
Oh, they totally believed it.
有人走到我面前对我说：“我以为你们俩挺不过去呢，我以为这只是一场大派对，别的什么也没有。”

00:11:10.900 --> 00:11:16.330
There are people who came up to me and they said, I didn't think you guys were going to make it and I thought it was just going to be a big party and nothing else.
我们进行到哪儿了？

00:11:17.120 --> 00:11:17.620
Where are we at?
我们还在20分。

00:11:18.500 --> 00:11:19.740
We're still at 20.
停留在20分。

00:11:20.700 --> 00:11:21.520
Holding at 20.
你们婚礼上另一个不寻常的时刻——这在婚礼中绝对很不传统——就是你们谈到了洗手间。我们谈到了吗？我不记得这个了，你在说什么？谁在洗手间里待的时间更长，卡尔还是温迪？温迪。我也这么说。温迪，你呢？绝对是卡尔。等等。如果你看过他的洗手间，看到它比我的干净多少，你就会知道他在里面花更多时间，至少是在打扫卫生。

00:11:24.500 --> 00:11:55.260
another unusual moment in your ceremony that is certainly not very traditional in a wedding is that you talk about the bathroom what did we I don't remember this what are you talking about who spends more time in the bathroom Carl Wendy Wendy I'd say that too Wendy what do you say absolutely Carl wait a minute If you saw his bathroom and you saw how much cleaner it is than mine, you'd know he spent more time in there at least cleaning.
说得好，卡尔。

00:11:56.040 --> 00:11:56.960
That's good, Carl.
是的，但如果你看到她洗手间里所有的填字游戏和书，你就会明白了。

00:11:57.020 --> 00:12:01.640
Yes, but if you saw all the crossword puzzles and books that were in her bathroom, you'd know.
你知道，这绝对就像是，你知道的，一个不会在许多婚礼仪式上出现的画面。

00:12:02.620 --> 00:12:06.460
You know, it's definitely like, you know, an image that doesn't come up in many wedding ceremonies.
你知道的，这绝对就像是一个在许多婚礼仪式上不会出现的画面。

00:12:08.520 --> 00:12:09.260
I don't know.
我不知道。

00:12:09.280 --> 00:12:09.820
So what are you saying?
那你到底是什么意思？

00:12:09.880 --> 00:12:11.130
It's like this toilet taboo.
就像这个厕所的禁忌一样。

00:12:11.280 --> 00:12:12.280
It shouldn't have been mentioned.
本来就不该提起的。

00:12:12.500 --> 00:12:14.220
I'm just pointing out the facts.
我只是在指出事实。

00:12:14.280 --> 00:12:18.880
Look, I'm just being factual about what happened and what was traditional and what wasn't.
听着，我只是在实事求是地谈论发生了什么、什么是传统、什么不是传统。

00:12:19.040 --> 00:12:20.360
That's all I'm interested in saying.
我只想表达这些。

00:12:20.480 --> 00:12:23.860
There was only one question about our sex life, you know, sort of.
关于我们的性生活只有一个问题，你知道的，差不多吧。

00:12:25.080 --> 00:12:29.300
Name the movie title that best describes your love life.
说出一个最能形容你爱情生活的电影名。

00:12:31.720 --> 00:12:32.140
Okay.
好吧。

00:12:35.020 --> 00:12:35.780
Go ahead first.
你先来。

00:12:36.040 --> 00:12:36.440
You go.
你来。

00:12:36.560 --> 00:12:38.180
I said Best Friends.
我说的是《最佳损友》。

00:12:38.500 --> 00:12:39.160
Best Friends.
《最佳损友》。

00:12:40.500 --> 00:12:41.920
Burt Reynolds, Goldie Hawn.
伯特·雷诺兹、歌蒂·韩。

00:12:42.320 --> 00:12:43.260
Burt Reynolds, Goldie Hawn.
伯特·雷诺兹、歌蒂·韩。

00:12:44.040 --> 00:12:44.660
And Wendy?
温迪呢？

00:12:45.460 --> 00:12:46.520
Gone with the Wind.
《乱世佳人》。

00:12:46.580 --> 00:12:48.920
Well, let's go on with the ten points, too.
好吧，我们接着看那十条吧。

00:12:51.780 --> 00:12:52.940
We've been together eight years.
我们已经在一起八年了。

00:12:53.120 --> 00:12:53.720
I mean, you know.
我的意思是，你知道的。

00:12:53.900 --> 00:12:54.240
Right.
对。

00:12:56.380 --> 00:12:58.240
My main concern was that it was funny.
我最关心的其实是它是不是很有趣。

00:12:58.380 --> 00:12:59.400
That's all I cared about.
我只在乎这个。

00:12:59.560 --> 00:13:01.380
As long as we got laughs, I was happy.
只要能逗大家笑，我就很高兴。

00:13:02.140 --> 00:13:06.020
So I answered questions that I knew would hopefully get laughs, and luckily they did.
所以我回答那些我知道希望能逗笑大家的问题，幸运的是，它们确实做到了。

00:13:06.320 --> 00:13:07.620
But I didn't care about it.
但我根本不在乎别的。

00:13:07.640 --> 00:13:08.200
I wasn't nervous.
我一点也不紧张。

00:13:08.320 --> 00:13:10.560
I didn't care about marrying, you know, the wrong guy.
我才不在乎是不是嫁错了人呢。

00:13:10.940 --> 00:13:13.010
I knew I was with the right guy, and I knew I was in the right place.
我知道我和对的人在一起，也知道我在对的地方。

00:13:13.160 --> 00:13:17.740
So all I really cared about was the entertainment value of the game portion of the evening, really.
所以，我真正在乎的其实是当晚游戏环节的娱乐价值。

00:13:17.860 --> 00:13:18.820
That's all I thought about.
我只想了这些。

00:13:20.180 --> 00:13:32.540
And the producer in me was worried that it was going too slowly, that he wasn't getting the right camera angles, and, you know, oh, yeah, the questions, yeah, I'm not worried about that, but it was the show part and that people were having a good time.
而我身上那种制作人的本能，则担心进度太慢，担心摄影师没抓对角度，还有，哦对，那些问题，好吧，我不担心那个，但这是节目本身，而且大家玩得很开心。

00:13:33.140 --> 00:13:34.840
Yeah, I wish we had more cameras, actually.
对，其实我希望我们有更多摄像机。

00:13:35.980 --> 00:13:36.800
That would be good.
那就更好了。

00:13:37.140 --> 00:13:41.860
But you buy the hair stuff and the cleaning stuff and the moisturizer.
但你买美发用品、清洁用品还有保湿霜。

00:13:42.100 --> 00:13:43.780
Okay, so we're going to have to move this along.
好了，我们得加快进度了。

00:13:43.820 --> 00:13:44.500
You've got to get married.
你们得结婚了。

00:13:44.740 --> 00:13:45.080
Come on.
拜托。

00:13:45.460 --> 00:13:46.440
Well, maybe not.
好吧，也许不用。

00:13:47.260 --> 00:13:47.720
Maybe not.
也许不用。

00:13:47.840 --> 00:13:48.380
That's true.
也对。

00:13:48.580 --> 00:13:49.160
This is true.
确实如此。

00:13:49.380 --> 00:13:53.580
When I heard what you were doing, I mean, there was a part of me where I was just like, wow, they are amazing.
当我听说你们在做什么时，我的内心其实有一种感觉，就像是，哇，他们太厉害了。

00:13:53.820 --> 00:13:56.360
And there was a part of me which is just like, are they nuts?
但同时又有一种感觉，就像是，他们疯了吗？

00:13:57.720 --> 00:13:59.600
Well, what would be amazing about it?
好吧，这有什么厉害的？

00:13:59.620 --> 00:14:00.560
What would be nuts about it?
哪里疯了？

00:14:01.640 --> 00:14:11.540
Well, because a wedding at some point, I mean, I think it has to be about love, about this, you know, just about this feeling between the two of you, you know?
嗯，因为婚礼在某种程度上，我的意思是，我认为它必须关于爱，关于这个，你知道的，仅仅关于你们两人之间的这种感觉，你知道吗？

00:14:12.360 --> 00:14:16.120
And the context of, you know, your typical game show doesn't usually make the space for that.
而你们那种典型游戏节目的语境，通常并不会为这种感觉留出空间。

00:14:17.140 --> 00:14:22.550
I mean, I've been to some weddings, some of our friends, and I just thought they were beautiful and romantic.
我的意思是，我参加过一些婚礼，是我们一些朋友的，我当时觉得它们既美丽又浪漫。

00:14:22.600 --> 00:14:24.680
And I thought, wow, I would love to do that.
我还想，哇，我也好想办一场那样的。

00:14:24.760 --> 00:14:26.600
But I also thought that that really wasn't us.
但我也觉得那其实并不适合我们。

00:14:26.720 --> 00:14:29.780
I mean, it's not how we deal with each other.
我的意思是，这不是我们相处的方式。

00:14:29.860 --> 00:14:35.500
Not that we're not romantic and love each other, but we just express it in a different way.
并不是说我们不浪漫、不相爱，只是我们表达的方式不同。

00:14:36.260 --> 00:14:38.600
You know, I've been to some weddings that really sucked.
你知道，我参加过一些糟糕透顶的婚礼。

00:14:38.800 --> 00:14:41.160
I mean, you know, I mean, come on.
我是说，你知道的，拜托。

00:14:41.180 --> 00:14:46.540
There have been some totally lame-ass weddings at a banquet hall in, you know, Lamont, Illinois, or Joliet.
有些婚礼简直烂透了，就在伊利诺伊州拉蒙特或朱利叶的某个宴会厅里。

00:14:46.880 --> 00:14:48.600
They go on for an hour and a half.
一办就是一个半小时。

00:14:48.600 --> 00:14:51.150
Yeah, and people think they're romantic, and they're just boring.
对，人们觉得它们很浪漫，但实际上无聊透顶。

00:14:51.800 --> 00:14:57.360
So, you know, anyone could, you know, anyone could do what it takes to, quote, unquote, have a romantic wedding.
所以，你知道的，任何人都能做到所谓的拥有一个浪漫婚礼所需的一切。

00:14:57.460 --> 00:14:58.600
It's just like making soup.
这就像做汤一样。

00:14:58.740 --> 00:14:59.540
You know, you have the right ingredients.
你知道的，你备好正确的食材。

00:15:00.020 --> 00:15:00.970
You throw in the flowers.
扔进鲜花。

00:15:01.040 --> 00:15:01.940
You throw in the dress.
扔进婚纱。

00:15:02.000 --> 00:15:05.600
You throw in someone playing a song from Fiddler on the Roof or whatever.
扔进一个弹奏《屋顶上的提琴手》或者别的什么曲子的人。

00:15:05.820 --> 00:15:06.480
You just, you know, you throw in all that.
你只是，你知道的，把所有这些都扔进去。

00:15:06.480 --> 00:15:07.840
I'm not doing any wedding for my family.
我才不会为了我的家人办什么婚礼。

00:15:08.080 --> 00:15:11.800
Well, yeah, it's like you throw in all the usual crap, and that's supposed to be romantic.
好吧，对，就像你把所有寻常的垃圾都扔进去，然后这就成了所谓的浪漫。

00:15:12.370 --> 00:15:13.820
Well, that's, you know, that's not true.
好吧，那，你知道的，并不是这样的。

00:15:14.320 --> 00:15:20.000
And nobody, I don't think anybody really said, people actually said to me, this is exactly the wedding I thought you would have.
而且没人，我觉得根本没人这么说过，实际上有人对我说：“这正是我想象中你们会办的婚礼。”

00:15:20.680 --> 00:15:22.540
And that, to me, says everything right there.
对我来说，这句话说明了一切。

00:15:23.620 --> 00:15:24.740
Was it romantic at all?
它有一点浪漫吗？

00:15:26.960 --> 00:15:41.360
I think the most romantic part, and maybe it wasn't for the audience, but for me, and maybe for us, because it was very romantic during the actual ceremony itself when the judge broke it all down to what it was really all about.
我觉得最浪漫的部分——也许对观众来说不是，但对我来说，也许对我们来说是，因为在真正的婚礼仪式进行期间非常浪漫，当法官把这一切剥离，还原到它真正的本质时。

00:15:42.010 --> 00:15:45.600
When he said that the fact that we had found each other was a miracle.
当他说我们能找到彼此是个奇迹的时候。

00:15:45.740 --> 00:15:54.400
I mean, it is unusual that two very different people found each other through the biggest medium in the world, which is television.
我的意思是，两个非常不同的人通过世界上最大媒介——也就是电视——找到了彼此，这很不寻常。

00:15:54.640 --> 00:16:01.620
And it brought us together and it brought a whole bunch of people that we love together that wouldn't normally know each other.
它把我们聚在了一起，也把一群我们爱的人聚在了一起，这些人平时根本不会认识彼此。

00:16:01.620 --> 00:16:01.720
there.
在那儿。

00:16:02.020 --> 00:16:04.760
I don't think you could say that there's a traditional romance.
我觉得你不能说这就是传统意义上的浪漫。

00:16:05.360 --> 00:16:11.120
I mean, this is, to make it romantic is kind of to do what you want to do and to do what means the most to you.
我的意思是，要让它变得浪漫，某种程度上就是去做你想做的事，去做对你意义最重大事。

00:16:11.290 --> 00:16:12.450
And I think we achieved that.
我想我们做到了这一点。

00:16:12.760 --> 00:16:15.660
So for me, it was very romantic because it's what we wanted to do.
所以对我来说，它非常浪漫，因为这就是我们想做的事。

00:16:17.380 --> 00:16:24.100
Yeah, I was, I, the most romantic moment was just standing there when we were looking in each other's eyes.
对，我，最浪漫的时刻就是静静地站在那里，四目相对。

00:16:24.870 --> 00:16:25.140
You know what?
你知道吗？

00:16:25.160 --> 00:16:26.780
I actually wanted to tell the judge to stop.
我其实想让法官停下来。

00:16:26.940 --> 00:16:28.080
I just want to tell him to stop.
我只想让他停下来。

00:16:28.080 --> 00:16:33.140
And I just wanted to stand there for a minute, just frozen, just remembering that moment.
我只想在那里站上一会儿，就像定格一样，只为记住那一刻。

00:16:33.780 --> 00:16:35.140
Because it was all going by too quickly.
因为这一切过得太快了。

00:16:35.700 --> 00:16:39.080
And I knew we were going to run out of videotape, so I didn't do that.
而且我知道我们的录像带快用完了，所以我没有这么做。

00:16:39.860 --> 00:16:40.940
Remember this moment in time.
记住此时此刻。

00:16:41.780 --> 00:16:45.540
Before this moment, you have been many things to one another.
在此之前，你们在彼此生命中扮演过许多角色。

00:16:46.660 --> 00:16:49.880
Acquaintance, friend, companion, lover, dancing partner, and even teacher.
相识、朋友、伴侣、爱人、舞伴，甚至是老师。

00:16:50.800 --> 00:16:53.860
Because you've learned much from one another in the time you've known each other.
