00:37:59.380 --> 00:38:00.080
Hey, Nancy.
“嘿，南希。”

00:38:00.120 --> 00:38:01.360
Her name is Nancy anyway.
不管怎样，她叫南希。

00:38:04.700 --> 00:38:06.180
What is that, like Latin?
那是什么，拉丁语吗？

00:38:08.750 --> 00:38:09.700
She the one with the red hat?
她是那个戴红帽子的吗？

00:38:10.200 --> 00:38:12.540
Hey, like a burning bush?
嘿，就像燃烧的荆棘？

00:38:13.260 --> 00:38:14.780
I would enjoy such a thing.
我会享受这样的事情。

00:38:16.480 --> 00:38:20.700
This reminded me of the times in my life where I'd gotten a wrong number and a man had answered.
这让我想起了我生命中打错电话而一个男人接听的那些时刻。

00:38:21.320 --> 00:38:26.140
Oh, wrong number, I'd say, and go to hang up, and suddenly the guy says, Hey, are you hot?
“哦，打错了，”我会说，正准备挂断，突然那家伙说：“嘿，你性感吗？”

00:38:27.300 --> 00:38:28.570
And it's not just strangers.
而且不只是陌生人。

00:38:29.500 --> 00:38:31.280
My male friends do this to me all the time.
我的男性朋友们总是对我做这种事。

00:38:31.500 --> 00:38:44.140
I'll be telling a story about a friend, that she just moved to a new neighborhood, that she's writing a dissertation on French critiques of Dutch genre painting in the 19th century, and suddenly they'll need to know right now, does she have a nice body?
我要讲一个关于我朋友的故事，她刚搬到一个新社区，正在写一篇关于19世纪法国对荷兰风俗画评论的博士论文，而别人突然马上就要知道，她的身材好不好？

00:38:45.320 --> 00:38:51.420
The last 30 years have done their damnedest to clean up men's mouths, and in some cases, in some contexts, it has succeeded.
过去30年里，人们使尽浑身解数来净化男人的嘴，而且在某些情况下、在某些语境下，它确实成功了。

00:38:52.840 --> 00:38:59.980
But even these guys, these hyper-educated, fully modern, and slightly nerdy guys, need their ten-minute perv fix.
但即使是这些家伙——这些受过高等教育、完全现代且略带书呆子气的家伙——也需要他们那十分钟的色情慰藉。

00:39:01.340 --> 00:39:03.980
And that, to me, seems harmless.
在我看来，这似乎是无伤大雅的。

00:39:08.040 --> 00:39:10.000
Sarah Miller, in New York.
萨拉·米勒（Sarah Miller），发自纽约。

00:39:20.700 --> 00:39:23.360
I'm a dog outside your door.
我是你门外的一只狗。

00:39:23.780 --> 00:39:26.980
I have been there since quarter to four.
我在那儿待到快四点。

00:39:27.820 --> 00:39:31.440
You are a cat looking intense.
你是一只目光犀利的猫。

00:39:31.820 --> 00:39:35.300
I bite your leg in self-defense.
我出于自卫咬了你的腿。

00:39:41.960 --> 00:39:45.260
Act 4, Nostalgia, The Final Frontier.
第四幕：怀旧，最后的边疆。

00:39:46.160 --> 00:39:51.740
In this program about people stuck in the wrong decade, We bring you now a story about somebody stuck as far back as anybody can possibly go.
在这个关于人们困在错误年代的节目中，我们现在为您讲述一个关于某个被困在尽可能最古老起点的人的故事。

00:39:51.880 --> 00:39:55.280
This is a story from Italo Calvino's amazing little book, Cosmic Comics.
这是一个出自伊塔洛·卡尔维诺（Italo Calvino）的神奇小册子《宇宙奇趣录》的故事。

00:39:55.470 --> 00:39:57.240
It begins with this little scientific explanation.
它以这样一个微小的科学解释开头。

00:39:58.240 --> 00:40:10.660
Through the calculations begun by Edwin P. Hubble on the galaxy's velocity of recession, we can now establish the moment when all the universe's matter was concentrated in a single point before it began to expand in space.
通过埃德温·P·哈勃（Edwin P. Hubble）对星系退行速度开始的计算，我们现在可以确定这样一个时刻：当时宇宙的所有物质都浓缩在一个单一点中，然后才开始在空间中膨胀。

00:40:11.820 --> 00:40:14.260
And after that, our story begins.
在那之后，我们的故事开始了。

00:40:15.100 --> 00:40:16.300
Naturally, we were all there.
自然，我们当时都在那里。

00:40:16.300 --> 00:40:49.530
where else could we have been nobody knew then that there could be space or time either what use did we have for time packed in there like sardines i say packed like sardines using a literary image in reality there wasn't even space to pack us into every point of each of us coincided with every point of each of the others in a single point which was where we all were in fact we didn't even bother one another except for personality differences because when space doesn't exist having somebody unpleasant like Mr. Pabur Pabur underfoot all the time is the most irritating thing.
除了那里我们还能在哪儿呢，当时谁也不知道还会有空间或时间，我们要时间有什么用呢，像沙丁鱼一样挤在那里，我说像沙丁鱼一样挤着，用的是文学意象，实际上甚至连给我们挤的空间都没有，我们每个人的每一个点都与其他人每个人的每一个点重合在一个单一点中，也就是我们所有人当时所在的地方，事实上我们甚至都不会互相打扰，除了个性上的差异，因为当空间不存在时，像帕布尔·帕布尔先生这样讨嫌的人整天在脚边晃荡，是最让人恼火的事情。

00:40:51.220 --> 00:40:52.400
How many of us were there?
我们当时有多少人？

00:40:53.060 --> 00:40:55.600
Oh, I was never able to figure that out, not even approximately.
哦，我从来没能算清楚过，连大致数量都算不出。

00:40:56.500 --> 00:41:01.920
To make a count, we would have had to move apart at least a little, and instead we all occupied the same point.
要想数一数，我们至少得稍微分开一点，然而我们却都占据着同一个点。

00:41:03.060 --> 00:41:06.770
Contrary to what you might think, it wasn't the sort of situation that encourages sociability.
与你想象的相反，那可不是那种能促进社交的情况。

00:41:08.160 --> 00:41:17.760
I know, for example, that in other periods, neighbors called on one another, but there, because of the fact that we were all neighbors, Nobody even said good morning or good evening to anybody else.
例如我所知道的，在其他时期，邻居们会互相串门，但在那里，由于我们所有人都是邻居，甚至没有人跟其他人说过一声早上好或晚上好。

00:41:19.600 --> 00:41:22.880
In the end, each of us associated only with a limited number of acquaintances.
最后，我们每个人只与有限数量的熟人交往。

00:41:23.420 --> 00:41:32.880
The ones I remember most are Mrs. Fink, her friend DeZwao, a family of immigrants by the name of Zazu, and Mr. Pabur Pabur, whom I just mentioned.
我记忆最深的是芬克太太（Mrs. Fink）、她的朋友德兹瓦奥（DeZwao）、一个名叫扎祖（Zazu）的移民家庭，以及我刚提到的帕布尔·帕布尔先生。

00:41:33.640 --> 00:41:41.000
There was also a cleaning woman, maintenance staff she was called, only one for the whole universe, since there was so little room.
还有一个清洁工，当时叫后勤人员，整个宇宙只有一个，因为空间太小了。

00:41:42.300 --> 00:41:45.200
To tell the truth, she had nothing to do all day long, not even dusting.
说实话，她整天无所事事，连擦灰都不用。

00:41:45.840 --> 00:41:48.200
Inside one point, not even a grain of dust can enter.
在一个点里面，连一粒灰尘都进不去。

00:41:48.850 --> 00:41:51.200
So she spent all her time gossiping and complaining.
所以她把所有时间都花在了八卦和抱怨上。

00:41:52.840 --> 00:41:55.320
Just with the people I've already named, it would have been overcrowded.
光是我刚才点到的那些人，就已经拥挤不堪了。

00:41:55.790 --> 00:41:58.440
But you have to add all the stuff we had to keep piled up in there.
但你还得加上我们不得不堆在那里的所有东西。

00:41:59.300 --> 00:42:15.820
All the material it was to serve afterwards to form the universe, now dismantled and concentrated in such a way that you weren't able to tell what was later to become part of astronomy, like the nebula of Andromeda, from what was assigned to geography, the Vosges, for example, or to chemistry, like certain beryllium isotopes.
所有那些后来将用来组成宇宙的物质，当时被拆解并以这样一种方式浓缩着：你根本无法分辨什么后来会成为天文学的一部分（比如仙女座星云），什么会被分派到地理学（例如孚日山脉），或者化学（比如某些铍同位素）。

00:42:17.180 --> 00:42:23.580
And on top of that, we were always bumping against the Zizou family's household goods, camp beds, mattresses, baskets.
最重要的是，我们总是撞到扎祖一家的家居用品、野营床、床垫、篮子。

00:42:24.840 --> 00:42:31.740
These Zizous, if you weren't careful, with the excuse that they were a large family, would begin to act as if they were the only ones in the world.
这些扎祖一家，如果你不注意的话，就会借口说他们是一个大家庭，开始表现得好像他们是世界上仅有的人一样。

00:42:32.000 --> 00:42:35.480
They even wanted to hang lines across our point to dry their washing.
他们甚至想在我们的点里拉起晾衣绳来晒衣服。

00:42:35.540 --> 00:43:03.000
but the others had also wronged the zoos to begin with by calling them immigrants on the pretext that since the others had been there first the zoos had come later this was mere unfounded prejudice that seems obvious to me because neither before nor after existed there any place to immigrate from but there were those who insisted that the concept of immigrant could be understood stood in the abstract, outside of space and time.
但其他人一开始也对扎祖一家做过不公的事，叫他们移民，借口是既然其他人先到那儿，扎祖一家是后来才来的，这纯粹是没有根据的偏见，在我看来这显而易见，因为无论之前还是之后都不存在任何可以移民过来的地方，但有些人坚称，移民的概念可以在抽象意义上、在时空之外被理解。

00:43:04.550 --> 00:43:08.070
It was what you might call a narrow-minded attitude, our outlook at that time.
你可以称这是一种思想狭隘的态度，也就是我们当时的视野。

00:43:08.780 --> 00:43:09.200
Very petty.
非常小家子气。

00:43:09.980 --> 00:43:12.320
The fault of the environment in which we had been reared.
这是我们所处的环境带来的过错。

00:43:13.620 --> 00:43:17.280
An attitude that, basically, has remained in all of us, mind you.
说实话，这种态度基本上一直留在我们所有人身上。

00:43:17.960 --> 00:43:18.980
Keeps cropping up even today.
时至今日仍在不断浮现。

00:43:19.510 --> 00:43:58.530
If two of us happen to meet, at the bus stop, in a movie house, at an international dentist's convention and start reminiscing about the old days we say hello at times somebody recognizes me at other times i recognize somebody and we probably start asking about this one and that one even if each remembers only a few of those remembered by the others and so we start in again on the old disputes the slanders the denigrations until somebody mentions mrs fink every conversation finally gets around to her then all of a sudden the pettiness is put aside and we feel uplifted, filled with a blissful, generous emotion.
如果我们中的两个人恰巧碰面，在公交车站、在电影院、在国际牙医大会上，开始回忆起过去的时光，我们有时会打招呼，有时别人认出了我，有时我认出了别人，我们可能会开始打听这个和那个，即使每个人只记得其他人所记得的一小部分，于是我们又开始重提当年的争端、中伤和诋毁，直到有人提到芬克太太，每次谈话最终都会扯到她身上，然后突然之间，那些小家子气被抛到了一边，我们感到心胸开阔，充满了幸福、慷慨的情感。

00:43:59.750 --> 00:44:04.160
Mrs. Fink, the only one that none of us has forgotten and that we all regret.
芬克太太，我们所有人唯一都没有忘记、并且我们所有人都怀念的人。

00:44:05.580 --> 00:44:06.540
Where has she ended up?
她最后去哪儿了？

00:44:08.120 --> 00:44:09.800
I have long since stopped looking for her.
我早就停止寻找她了。

00:44:10.360 --> 00:44:15.300
Mrs. Fink, her bosom, her thighs, her orange dressing gown.
芬克太太，她的胸怀、她的双腿、她的橙色晨衣。

00:44:17.160 --> 00:44:20.700
We'll never meet her again in this system of galaxies or in any other.
在这个星系系统或任何其他系统中，我们再也不会遇到她了。

00:44:22.820 --> 00:44:49.800
let me make one thing clear this theory that the universe after having reached an extremity of rarefaction will be condensed again has never convinced me and yet many of us are counting only on that continually making plans for the time when we'll all be back there again last month i went into the bar here on the corner and whom did i see mr pabur pabur what's new with you how do you happen to be in this neighborhood hood.
让我把一件事说清楚：这种认为宇宙在达到稀薄的极致后会再次凝缩的理论从来没有说服过我，然而我们当中有许多人正指望这一点，不断地为我们所有人将再次回到那里的时刻做计划，上个月我走进街角的酒吧，你猜我看到了谁——帕布尔·帕布尔先生，你最近怎么样，你怎么会来这附近。

00:44:50.560 --> 00:44:53.360
I learned that he's the agent for a plastics firm in Pavia.
我了解到他是帕维亚一家塑料公司的代理商。

00:44:54.340 --> 00:44:57.840
He's the same as ever, with his silver tooth, his loud suspenders.
他还是老样子，镶着一颗银牙，戴着夸张的背带。

00:44:58.300 --> 00:45:03.250
When we go back there, he said to me in a whisper, the thing we have to make sure of is this.
等我们回到那里去时，他低声对我说，我们必须确保的一点是这个。

00:45:03.720 --> 00:45:06.080
This time, certain people remain out.
这一次，某些人得被留在外面。

00:45:06.640 --> 00:45:07.520
You know what I mean.
你知道我的意思。

00:45:07.860 --> 00:45:08.820
Those zoos.
那些扎祖一家。

00:45:10.020 --> 00:45:17.140
I would have liked to answer him by saying, I've heard a number of people make the same remark, concluding, you know who I mean, Mr. Pabur Pabur.
我真想回答他说，我也听不少人说过同样的话，并以这句话结尾：你知道我指的是谁，帕布尔·帕布尔先生。

00:45:18.400 --> 00:45:22.420
To avoid the subject, I hastened to say, what about Mrs. Fink?
为了避开这个话题，我赶忙说道，芬克太太呢？

00:45:23.000 --> 00:45:24.900
Do you think we'll find her back there again?
你觉得我们还能在那里找到她吗？

00:45:26.420 --> 00:45:30.480
Ah, yes, she by all means, he said, turning purple.
啊，是的，她无论如何都会在的，他说着，脸涨成了紫色。

00:45:31.980 --> 00:45:38.120
For all of us, the hope of returning to that point means, above all, the hope of being once more with Mrs. Fink.
对于我们所有人来说，回归那个点的希望，首先意味着能够再次与芬克太太在一起的希望。

00:45:39.300 --> 00:45:42.060
This applies even to me, though I don't believe in it.
这也适用于我，尽管我不相信这一点。

00:45:43.060 --> 00:45:48.100
And in that bar, as always happens, we fell to talking about her, and were moved.
而在那家酒吧里，就像往常一样，我们开始谈论她，并且深受感动。

00:45:49.220 --> 00:45:52.540
Even Mr. Beber's unpleasantness faded in the face of that memory.
面对那段记忆，连贝贝尔先生的讨嫌也烟消云散了。

00:45:54.140 --> 00:45:59.500
Mrs. Fink's great secret is that she never aroused any jealousy among us, or any gossip either.
芬克太太伟大的秘密在于，她从未在我们中间激起任何嫉妒，也没有引起任何闲话。

00:46:00.490 --> 00:46:03.940
The fact that she went to bed with her friend, Mr. DeZwao, was well known.
她和她的朋友德兹瓦奥先生同床共枕是众所周知的。

00:46:04.600 --> 00:46:08.260
But in a point, if there's a bed, it takes up the whole point.
但在一个点里，如果有张床，它就会占满整个点。

00:46:09.620 --> 00:46:11.860
So it isn't a question of going to bed, but of being there.
所以这根本不是上床的问题，而是身处其中的问题。

00:46:12.340 --> 00:46:14.240
Because anybody in the point is also in the bed.
因为身处这个点中的任何人，也同样身处那张床上。

00:46:15.130 --> 00:46:18.200
Consequently, it was inevitable that she should be in bed also with each of us.
因此，不可避免地，她也与我们每个人都在一张床上。

00:46:19.300 --> 00:46:22.960
If she had been another person, there's no telling all the things that would have been said about her.
如果她是另一个人，真不知道关于她会有多少流言蜚语传出来呢。

00:46:23.380 --> 00:46:27.820
It was the cleaning woman who always started the slander, and the others didn't have to be coaxed to imitate her.
总是那个清洁工挑起流言蜚语，而其他人根本不需要劝说就会效仿她。

00:46:28.900 --> 00:46:33.680
On the subject of the Zazu family, for a change, the horrible things we had to hear.
作为换口味的话题，在扎祖一大家子的事上，我们不得不听那些可怕的事情。

00:46:34.340 --> 00:46:37.220
Father, daughters, brothers, sisters, mother, aunts.
父亲、女儿、兄弟、姐妹、母亲、姑姑。

00:46:38.120 --> 00:46:41.460
Nobody showed any hesitation even before the most sinister insinuation.
即使面对最阴险的影射，也没有人表现出丝毫犹豫。

00:46:42.680 --> 00:46:43.800
But with her it was different.
但对她却不同。

00:46:44.670 --> 00:46:53.240
The happiness I derived from her was the joy of being concealed, punctiform, in her, and of protecting her, punctiform, in me.
我从她身上获得的快乐，是那种将自己隐匿在点状的她之中、并在我这个点状的躯体中保护她的喜悦。

00:46:54.260 --> 00:47:04.700
It was at the same time vicious contemplation, thanks to the promiscuity of the punctiform convergence of all of us in her, and also chastity given her punctiform impenetrability.
这同时也是一种邪恶的凝视，多亏了我们所有人都在她体内点状汇聚的那种混杂性，同时也由于她那点状的不可穿透性而带有一种贞洁。

00:47:06.000 --> 00:47:07.980
In short, what more could I ask?
简而言之，我还能要求什么呢？

00:47:10.100 --> 00:47:15.160
And all of this, which was true of me, was also true for each of the others, and for her.
所有这些对我来说是真的，对其他每一个人以及对她来说也都是真的。

00:47:16.160 --> 00:47:21.760
She contained and was contained with equal happiness, and she welcomed us and loved us and inhabited all equally.
她以同样的快乐包容着并被包容着，她平等地欢迎我们、爱我们并栖息在所有人的心中。

00:47:23.420 --> 00:47:29.880
we got along so well all together, so well that something extraordinary was bound to happen.
我们大家相处得那么好，好到某种非同寻常的事情注定要发生。

00:47:30.790 --> 00:47:39.020
It was enough for her to say, at a certain moment, oh, if I only had some room, how I'd like to make some noodles for you boys.
只要她在某个时刻说上一句，哦，我要是能有点空间，该多想给你们这些小伙子做点面条啊。

00:47:40.360 --> 00:47:57.240
And in that moment, we all thought of the space that her round arms would occupy, moving backward and forward with a rolling pin over the dough, her bosom leaning over the great mound of flour and eggs which cluttered the wide board while her arms kneaded and kneaded, white and shiny with oil up to the elbows.
就在那一刻，我们所有人都想到了空间：她那圆润的手臂前后移动，用擀面杖在面团上擀着，她的胸膛俯在塞满了宽案板的面粉和鸡蛋堆上，而她的手臂不停地揉啊揉，白皙光亮，一直到胳膊肘都沾满了油。

00:47:59.540 --> 00:48:32.560
We thought of the space that the flower would occupy, and the wheat for the flower, and the fields to raise the wheat, and the mountains from which the water would flow to irrigate the fields, and the grazing lands for the herds of calves that would give their meat for the sauce, of the space it would take for the sun to arrive with its rays to ripen the wheat, of the space for the sun to condense from the clouds of stellar gases and burn, of the quantities of stars and galaxies and galactic masses in flight through space which would be needed to hold suspended every galaxy, every nebula, every sun, every planet.
我们想到了面粉所需的空间，制作面粉的小麦所需的空间，种植小麦的田野所需的空间，流淌出滋润田野的水的山脉所需的空间，以及提供肉酱原料的小牛群所需的牧场所需的空间，想到了太阳带着光芒到达那里以使小麦成熟所需的空间，想到了太阳从恒星气云中凝集并燃烧所需的空间，想到了在太空中飞行的星系、星云和星系团的数量——这些数量是悬挂每一个星系、每一个星云、每一个太阳、每一个行星所必需的。

00:48:33.660 --> 00:48:38.660
And at the same time we thought of it, this space was inevitably being formed.
正当我们这样想着的时候，这个空间正不可避免地形成。

00:48:39.520 --> 00:48:44.240
At the same time that Mrs. Fink was uttering those words, Ah, what noodles, boys!
就在芬克太太说出那些话的同时：啊，多好的面条啊，小伙子们！

00:48:44.960 --> 00:49:02.640
The point that contained her and all of us was expanding in a halo of distance in light years and light centuries and billions of light millennia, and we were being hurled to the four corners of the universe, Mr. Bur-bur-bur-bur all the way to Pavia, and she dissolved into I don't know what kind of energy light heat.
那个容纳了她和我们所有人的点，正在光年、光世纪和数十亿光年的耀眼距离中膨胀成一个光晕，而我们被抛向了宇宙的四个角落——布尔-布尔-布尔-布尔先生一直被抛到了帕维亚，而她则溶解成了我不知道是什么种类的能量、光和热。

00:49:03.700 --> 00:49:05.100
She, Mrs. Fink.
她，芬克太太。

00:49:06.340 --> 00:49:10.560
She who in the midst of our closed, petty world had been capable of a generous impulse.
她，在我们要好又狭隘的世界中间，曾怀有慷慨冲动的人。

00:49:11.220 --> 00:49:13.480
Boys, the noodles I would make for you.
小伙子们，我真想给你们做面条。

00:49:14.120 --> 00:49:46.500
A true outburst of general love, love, initiating at the same moment the concept of space, and properly speaking, space itself, and time, and universal gravitation, and the gravitating universe, making possible billions and billions of suns, and of planets, and fields of wheat, and Mrs. Finks, scattered through the continents of the planets, kneading with flowery, oil-shiny, generous arms, and she lost at that that very moment, and we mourning her loss.
这是一种全人类大爱的真正爆发，这种爱在同一时刻催生了空间的概念，严格来说就是空间本身、时间、万有引力以及引力宇宙，使数十亿计的太阳、行星以及小麦田成为可能，使散布在行星大陆上的芬克太太们成为可能——她们用沾满面粉、泛着油光、慷慨的手臂揉面，而她却恰恰在那个时刻消逝了，而我们则在哀悼她的失去。

